Only Wasm is substituted. The published ABI module identity and JS output name
are retained; Android and JVM continue using their published Compose artifacts.

Input fix: defer DOM text and character-selection synchronization while a native
edit batch is queued or being processed. After the whole batch commits, read the
current platform text-input request model and synchronize once, including rejected
or unchanged edits. Do not restore an intermediate model over native typing ahead
of the deferred Compose event queue. The composition guard remains in force.

Forward Delete uses the browser's authoritative beforeinput range exactly once
through existing edit commands. Suppress its keyboard route only for the matching
native edit; preserve the original modified-key fallback when word/line ranges
are unavailable. A collapsed content-delete fallback counts Unicode code points,
never individual surrogate units; word/line deletion never falls back to one code
point. Element-child range offsets are converted to text offsets.

No global DOM overrides, swallowed errors, clamped offsets, forced focus resets,
or duplicate forward-delete command. The private communicator reads the existing
platform request value after the batch; input ownership and lifecycle are retained.

Source rebuild compatibility (also required with original Kotlin 2.4.20):
- Synchronization.skiko: match the expect class's PublishedApi on its actual class.
- PlatformClipboard.wasm: infer the JsAny-bounded Promise await result rather than
  explicitly requesting Any?. Clipboard behavior and public API are unchanged.

Remove the input overlay after an official release synchronizes the live DOM
before selection and implements the native forward-delete protocol, then rerun
the trusted keyboard and DOM event-queue regressions.
